00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:51.100
Hi.

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:52.212
TAYLOR NGUYEN: Hi, Joanna.

00:00:52.212 --> 00:00:53.670
JOANNA SMITH: This
lounge is great.

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:55.440
You want to tell me
some fun facts about it?

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:57.440
TAYLOR NGUYEN: Welcome
to the Inclusion Lounge.

00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:59.900
And the purpose of
Inclusion Lounge

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:04.040
is to make sure that at Next
we're always providing content

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:07.760
and experiences to support
underrepresented groups

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:10.490
and allies, to be able
to come together, share

00:01:10.490 --> 00:01:13.430
learnings, collaborate,
and build community.

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:14.420
So, yeah.

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:17.030
It's a safe space,
and at anytime people

00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:20.750
could drop by, connect
with like-minded others,

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:24.230
get confidence coaching,
and also get headshots.

00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:26.840
And then in the
interim, we also have

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:29.600
sessions like I Am
Remarkable, which is going

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:30.905
on right around our shoulder.

00:01:30.905 --> 00:01:31.820
JOANNA SMITH: I
love that session.

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:33.560
TAYLOR NGUYEN: Yeah,
and this session

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:35.420
is happening a
couple times at Next.

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:37.730
And it takes us
through an exercise

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:41.450
of empowerment and learning
how to promote ourselves

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:42.597
in all the positive ways.

00:01:42.597 --> 00:01:44.180
JOANNA SMITH: What
do you think really

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:45.620
makes the Inclusion
Lounge stand out,

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:47.240
and why should people
think about coming here

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:48.150
during their day?

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:49.608
TAYLOR NGUYEN:
Yeah, you know what?

00:01:49.608 --> 00:01:51.278
It's not even about
thinking about it.

00:01:51.278 --> 00:01:52.820
It's just knowing
that it's available

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:55.940
because so much about
inclusion is you have

00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:57.350
to be ready to be in the space.

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:58.100
JOANNA SMITH: Yes.

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:00.110
TAYLOR NGUYEN: And when
you're ready to receive

00:02:00.110 --> 00:02:03.440
and you're ready to learn from
others, and become an ally

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:06.440
or become an advocate, that's
the time to actually visit.

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:08.289
And it shouldn't be
an intimidating space.

00:02:08.289 --> 00:02:09.997
It should be a space
where you could feel

00:02:09.997 --> 00:02:11.690
like you could be welcomed.

00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:14.300
You can meet like-minded people,
and you can actually learn

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:15.820
and listen from one another.

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:19.010
Our attendees are
always sharing with us

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:21.560
that whether they're an
introvert or an extrovert,

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:24.650
they need a place to
unwind and step away

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:27.740
from the commotion of Next and
all the wonderful experiences

00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:29.010
that are available here.

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:31.130
And then they're
really able to then go

00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:33.170
from a collaborative
mindset, rather

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:34.337
than an overwhelmed mindset.

00:02:34.337 --> 00:02:36.587
JOANNA SMITH: Thank you again
for building this space.

00:02:36.587 --> 00:02:37.740
I really admire it.

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:39.280
TAYLOR NGUYEN: Thanks for
coming to talk to us about it.

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:41.270
And always feel that
you could drop by

00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:43.220
and Inclusion Lounge
because we all know it's

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:45.830
really important at Next to
build a cloud for everyone.

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:47.030
Thanks everyone.

